menu "Checkpoint antenna"

    config CHECKPOINT_ANTENNA_IPEX
        bool "Boot on the IPEX antenna (Waveshare ESP32-C5-Zero only)"
        default n
        help
            Drives GPIO 26 high before the radio starts: on the C5-Zero it is the
            antenna switch, high for the IPEX connector, low for the onboard
            antenna. Off, the firmware leaves GPIO 26 alone and the board stays on
            its default, the onboard antenna. Only for a C5-Zero: GPIO 26 is
            something else, or nothing, on other boards. The boot calibration and
            K i's automatic recalibration see that antenna: on the bench, K then i
            switches the antenna at run time and recalibrates every LO on it. A
            boot with nothing on the IPEX connector is deaf.

endmenu

menu "Checkpoint detector"

    config CHECKPOINT_PAIR_GUARD
        bool "Hold a pair's dominated reading on saturated captures"
        default y
        help
            One capture carries two Raceband channels, each in the other's image
            window. A drone close enough to drive the ADC into its rails makes the
            partner channel read the rails' products (host model: a median 23-29
            dB under the strong channel), which rang phantom passes on the bench
            (a 25 mW VTX within about 30 cm of the onboard antenna at gain 40).

            On, a saturated capture's reading of a channel whose smoothed level
            stands more than 15 dB under its partner's is held, not fed. After a
            jump into the rails (a VTX switched on or armed beside the antenna,
            its average still low), the source is the channel whose last 3
            readings show it (their median), and its partner is held until the
            run ends. A hover (a run of saturated captures over 150 ms) holds
            30 ms longer after each one. A channel held over 0.5 s starts
            again from the level it comes back at, once its fresh average has
            settled (0.3 s of readings at the default alpha, ringing nothing
            meanwhile; a shorter hold pauses it): armed under the release;
            over it, relatively armed there, or in
            COOLDOWN until it falls under the release with
            CHECKPOINT_REARM_DROP_DB at 0. Off, every reading is fed as it
            comes, the phantoms included. The rules:
            docs/detector.md, "Pair ghost guard", and scan_detector.h.

            Its limits:
            - The partner channel is blind while the strong one clips: about
              80 ms for 600 mW passing 0.3 m away at 20 m/s (host model). A real
              pass on it inside that window is timed from what follows: up to
              about 70 ms off, and lost when it is 45 dB weaker (host model).
            - The blind window grows as 1/speed: about 310 ms at 5 m/s, where
              a partner 20-30 dB weaker crossing at the same instant rang on
              time in 5 runs of 20 and 150-170 ms late in the others (host
              model).
            - It grows with the link gain too: the IPEX connector with a better
              antenna, or a directional one, clips from further out (about
              870 ms at 5 m/s with about 8 dB more, host model).
            - A jump names its source only while the partner reads more than
              15 dB under the source on the rails, about 40 dB over the floor
              at most. A partner higher than that (a quad left powered about
              1 m from the antenna while another is armed beside it) leaves the
              source held for its whole run: its own onset rings nothing, the
              partner's laps are kept (host model).
            - Two drones at the gate together: a drone that crosses close while
              another one's slow pass clips can be named the source partway
              through it. The clipping drone is then held to the end of its run
              and loses its pass when over 0.5 s of it is left (host model).
            - It keys on the saturated flag only: a compression before the
              ADC rails (no rail hit, no flag) is not covered. Bench B11
              checks whether the board does that.
            - Held for 1 s (a drone parked by the gate), the channel reads
              unknown in STATS.
            - The IPEX build (detector-ipex) keeps this default for now: decide
              its default after bench B9 measures the IPEX link.

    config CHECKPOINT_REARM_DROP_DB
        int "Relative re-arm: drop under the last pass, dB (0 = off)"
        range 0 40
        default 16
        help
            A channel re-arms after a pass once the refractory period is over and
            its level is back under active_db - hysteresis_db. A drone that stays
            well up between laps never gets there: a 25 mW VTX held 3 m away
            indoors reads about +30 dB (bench), a 600 mW drone 30-80 m away
            outdoors 15-23 dB (host model), so every lap after the first is lost.

            With a drop D over 0, the channel also re-arms once the refractory
            period is over and its 1 s average stands D under the highest level
            since the pass. The next pass must then rise D over the lowest 1 s
            average since that re-arm, as well as pass active_db and min_peak_db.
            Falling under the release ends it: the channel is then armed as with 0.
            0 is the old behaviour, to the bit (host test). The rule and the
            simulation: docs/detector.md, "Relative re-arm".

            The default is the host simulation's: total lap errors (missed and
            extra) are lowest for D 14-15 with mild fading and 16-18 with rough
            fading, and 16 is the smallest D that rings no extra pass on the
            bench's recording of a VTX held at 3 m. Its limits (host model):
            - A lap whose gate pass stands less than about D + 2 dB over the far
              side of the track is mostly lost: an indoor 25 mW track with the
              antenna 1-3 m from the line, a 600 mW drone indoors, the IPEX
              antenna (its gate pass reaches the ADC ceiling sooner). Put the
              antenna at the gate (the drone within 1 m) or lower D.
            - A drone parked near the gate rings an extra pass when its level
              swings by D and back: at D 16, 0.03 per 10 s hover, none for a
              still drone (a crash, the start pad), but about 1 per 30 s on the
              pad if it wobbles like the bench's hand-held VTX (5.3 dB); a
              lower D rings more (D 12: 0.4-0.6 per hover).
            - A track that comes back within a few metres of the gate can ring
              there too, as the old re-arm would if the drone fell under the
              release.
            Not saved in NVS and not on the link: a different D is a different
            build (sdkconfig.local.defaults), and the boot line shows it
            (rearm_db=).

endmenu

menu "Checkpoint C5<->C3 link"

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        bool "Enable the UART link to the C3 config/telemetry bridge"
        default y
        help
            Report pass events and stats to, and accept detector configuration
            from, the bridge (a C3 node or the C6 master) over UART. With it
            off, passes appear only as PASS lines on the console, which is then
            the only way to tune the detector (it has no local output).

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_UART_NUM
        int "UART controller number"
        depends on CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        default 1
        range 0 1
        help
            The console is on USB-Serial-JTAG, so UART1 (or UART0) is free.

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_TX_GPIO
        int "Link UART TX GPIO (to the C3 RX)"
        depends on CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        default 6
        help
            GPIO 6 (TX) and 8 (RX) are header pins on the C5-Zero (GPIO 15 is
            not broken out). GPIO 8 is free on the detector (the dump engine
            uses no GPIO). See the GPIO map in CLAUDE.md.

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_RX_GPIO
        int "Link UART RX GPIO (from the C3 TX)"
        depends on CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        default 8

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_BAUD
        int "Link UART baud rate"
        depends on CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        default 115200

    config CHECKPOINT_LINK_STATS_MS
        int "Stats report period (ms)"
        depends on CHECKPOINT_LINK_ENABLE
        default 1000

endmenu
